const report=`# Civication — Subkultur / Program og koordinering prerequisites\n\nThis package materializes the playable prerequisite foundation for \`${ROLE}\`. It is **not Role World completion** and does not add new runtime state.\n\n## Source-first scope\n- Existing canonical role model and work grammar are extended rather than replaced.\n- Persistent work object: \`${PERSIST}\`.\n- Four fictional scenario actors: booking/artist contact, economy/contracts, local scene/partners, communication/publication.\n- Four role-owned work surfaces keep criteria, booking/contract/cost, partner representation and publication/logistics separate but version-connected.\n- 15 authored mails across all 9 canonical mail types; deterministic 16-step plan; no generic fallback.\n- History Go: Club 7 / \`club_7_vika\` is a bounded historical program-and-milieu affordance only. It cannot prescribe current booking, grant program entitlement, approve fee/contract/rights, set capacity or create safety authority.\n- Cross-role remains \`candidate_when_shared_work_is_real\`; no shared work object or cross-role runtime is materialized merely because producer, production lead or arena roles are plausible collaborators.\n\n## Authority\nProgram coordination may compare alternatives, coordinate offers and hold publication when prerequisites are missing. It may not promise booking/program place without mandate, hide real cost or expected unpaid work, use subcultural status/friendship as access criteria, publish unresolved status as confirmed, or invent legal/rights/economic/employer/safety authority.\n\n## Quality gate\n29/30 before PR browser boot. The final point is reserved for exact-head Chromium boot/typecheck CI.\n`;
write('reports/CIVICATION_SUBKULTUR_PROGRAM_OG_KOORDINERING_PREREQUISITES_SOURCE_FIRST.md',report);
